    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112866" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φώσσων</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φώσων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a coarse linen
				garment,</i> used in Egypt, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.71
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν φώσωνι τὴν ἴσην ἔχων μετ᾽ ἐμοῦ
					διῆγες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cratin.
					250
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>sail, sail-cloth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1151.12
			</span></i>. (Perh. Egyptian.)</div>
